Package: koserver
Architecture: any
# No ${shlibs:Depends}: the binary is a statically linked Go build
# (CGO_ENABLED=0, pure-Go SQLite driver), so it has no dynamic library
# dependencies for dh_shlibdeps to compute.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: self-hosted, wire-compatible KOReader sync server
 koserver is a drop-in replacement for the official KOReader sync
 server (sync.koreader.rocks): it implements the same register/auth/
 progress-push-pull API, so the KOReader app can point at it without
 any change in behavior.
 .
 On top of that it adds a self-service web UI (account creation,
 password change, password recovery), an admin panel, and an admin
 CLI baked into the same binary. Data is stored in a local SQLite
 database.
 .
 This package installs koserver as a systemd service running under
 its own unprivileged system user; see /etc/koserver/koserver.env for
 configuration.
